"{\"state\":\"done\",\"baseline\":0,\"newEntryCount\":7,\"newEntries\":[{\"kind\":\"user\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"Explain the course calculation for a 9.80 m rafter run with 5 m sheets and a 200 mm end lap. State how many courses are needed and show the arithmetic you used.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read_workflow_route\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"version\\\":\\\"xray.workflow/1\\\",\\\"workflow\\\":\\\"discussion\\\",\\\"steps\\\":[\\\"Discuss capabilities or plans; do not claim project actions occurred.\\\"],\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Workflow selection only; no geometry, evidence or authority changed.\\\"}\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"use the project's roof-sheet coverage tool to get the authoritative arithmetic, then present the steps.\\n\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"calculate_draft_roof_sheet_coverage\",\"failed\":true,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"Invalid tool arguments: supplierReference: Invalid input: expected string, received undefined; : Unrecognized key: \\\"suplierReference\\\"\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"I had a typo in the parameter name. Let me retry with the correct field.\\n\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"calculate_draft_roof_sheet_coverage\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"projectId\\\":\\\"job-1bf6dd91-608b-4e4f-ab11-0a357875a38d\\\",\\\"projectRevision\\\":1,\\\"status\\\":\\\"draft-sheet-coverage\\\",\\\"columns\\\":14,\\\"courses\\\":2,\\\"sheets\\\":28,\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"developedWidthM\\\":\\\"10.0\\\",\\\"developedRunM\\\":\\\"9.8\\\",\\\"effectiveCoverM\\\":\\\"0.762\\\",\\\"orderLengthM\\\":\\\"5.0\\\",\\\"endLapM\\\":\\\"0.2\\\",\\\"measurementReference\\\":\\\"Rafter run 9.80 m supplied by the user for course calculation only; developed width and effective cover are illustrative (typical corrugated profile) and not user-specified — used only so the tool can run.\\\",\\\"supplierReference\\\":\\\"Sheet order length 5.000 m and end lap 0.200 m supplied by the user; supplier not named.\\\"},\\\"calculation\\\":{\\\"columns\\\":\\\"ceil(10.0 / 0.762) = 14\\\",\\\"coursesFormula\\\":\\\"run <= ordered length ? 1 : 1 + ceil((run - ordered length) / (ordered length - end lap))\\\",\\\"courses\\\":\\\"1 + ceil((9.8 - 5.0) / (5.0 - 0.2)) = 2\\\",\\\"coursesExpanded\\\":\\\"Course 1 covers a full ordered sheet length of 5.0 m. The remaining 4.8 m is covered by further courses that each add 5.0 - 0.2 = 4.8 m, so ceil(4.8 / 4.8) = 1 more course(s), giving 2 courses in total.\\\",\\\"courseBoundary\\\":\\\"2 course(s) cover any run greater than 5 m and up to and including exactly 9.8 m. A run of 9.800000001 m or more needs at least 3 courses.\\\",\\\"boundaryPrecision\\\":\\\"The next boundary value uses this calculator's nine-decimal-place input resolution in metres. It does not establish measurement accuracy or PDF coordinate precision.\\\",\\\"maxRunAtThisCourseCountM\\\":9.8,\\\"minRunForAnotherCourseM\\\":9.800000001,\\\"wrongFormulaWarning\\\":\\\"Do NOT compute courses as ceil(run / (ordered length - end lap)); for this input that would give 3 instead of the correct 2, because the first course is not shortened by an end lap.\\\",\\\"sheets\\\":\\\"14 columns × 2 courses = 28 sheets\\\",\\\"orderedLength\\\":\\\"28 sheets × 5.0 m = 140 m\\\",\\\"endLapPolicy\\\":\\\"The first course covers a full ordered sheet length. Each additional course adds ordered length minus end lap.\\\",\\\"excessRun\\\":\\\"9.8 m covered run - 9.8 m requested run = 0 m excess run. This is geometric over-coverage along the run, not a per-sheet waste or cutting quantity.\\\"},\\\"cuttingSchedule\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"not-calculated\\\",\\\"perSheetWasteM\\\":null,\\\"reusableOffcuts\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No cutting layout, trimming or offcut reuse is supplied. Do not infer per-sheet waste, scrap, usable cut length or reusable offcuts from coverage excess, in either the answer or Developer review.\\\"},\\\"orderedLinearM\\\":140,\\\"coveredWidthM\\\":10.668,\\\"coveredRunM\\\":9.8,\\\"excessWidthM\\\":0.668,\\\"excessRunM\\\":0,\\\"measurementReference\\\":\\\"Rafter run 9.80 m supplied by the user for course calculation only; developed width and effective cover are illustrative (typical corrugated profile) and not user-specified — used only so the tool can run.\\\",\\\"supplierReference\\\":\\\"Sheet order length 5.000 m and end lap 0.200 m supplied by the user; supplier not named.\\\",\\\"verifiedQuoteEligible\\\":false,\\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"End lap (the lengthwise lap between courses, also called a transverse lap) IS included in this calculation: every course after the first is shortened by the supplied end lap. Do not describe end laps or transverse laps as excluded.\\\",\\\"Side lap (the lap between adjacent sheets across the width) is NOT calculated here: it is already contained in the supplied effective sheet cover, so it is neither added nor deducted again. Side lap and end lap are separate laps and must be explained separately.\\\",\\\"One rectangular developed surface with identical ordered sheet lengths; no opening deductions, hips, valleys, cutting or reusable offcut schedule.\\\",\\\"No fixings, flashings, product suitability or compliance calculation. References are retained but not validated; draft and not eligible for verified quotes.\\\"]}\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"## Course count\\n\\nTwo courses.\\n\\n## Arithmetic (the way the tool works)\\n\\n1. First course = full ordered sheet length, so it covers 5.000 m of run — no end lap is deducted from the first course.\\n2. Remaining run = 9.800 − 5.000 = 4.800 m.\\n3. Every course after the first adds (ordered length − end lap) = 5.000 − 0.200 = 4.800 m of effective run.\\n4. Additional courses = ceil(4.800 / 4.800) = ceil(1.000) = 1.\\n5. Total courses = 1 (first) + 1 (additional) = 2.\\n\\n## Common trap to avoid\\n\\nDo not compute `ceil(run / (ordered length − end lap))` = `ceil(9.8 / 4.8)` = `ceil(2.042)` = 3. That overcounts by one because the first course is not shortened by an end lap.\\n\\n## Boundary for these exact inputs\\n\\nTwo courses cover any run greater than 5 m and up to exactly 9.800 m. A run of 9.800000001 m or more needs at least 3 courses. To check a different run, recalculate — do not predict.\\n\\n## Caveats\\n\\n- This is end-lap (also called transverse-lap) coverage along the run and is included in the course count. Side lap is already inside the supplied effective cover and is a separate lap — do not describe end or transverse laps as excluded.\\n- No cutting layout, per-sheet waste, offcuts, hips, valleys, openings or fixings are calculated here. Only the course count for the run is supplied.\\n- Draft calculation only; not eligible for a verified quote.\\n\\n## Developer review\\n\\n- **Outcome:** Answered clearly — 2 courses, with correct first-course-is-full arithmetic and the wrong-formula trap flagged.\\n- **Friction:** Tool needs width/cover for run-only questions; I labelled those illustrative, which adds noise.\\n- **Improvement:** A run-only mode would let course-count questions run without illustrative width inputs.\"}],\"projectId\":\"job-1bf6dd91-608b-4e4f-ab11-0a357875a38d\",\"activeId\":\"2a57759c-c549-4295-a7ac-183124358f07\",\"threads\":2,\"busy\":false,\"error\":null,\"workPacket\":{\"state\":\"review-required\",\"objective\":\"Explain the course calculation for a 9.80 m rafter run with 5 m sheets and a 200 mm end lap. State how many courses are needed and show the arithmetic you used.\",\"nextAction\":\"Workflow receipts complete. Review the draft against its sources and acceptance tests; no professional approval or issue recorded.\",\"pendingAction\":null,\"routingFailure\":null},\"entries\":[{\"kind\":\"user\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"Explain the course calculation for a 9.80 m rafter run with 5 m sheets and a 200 mm end lap. State how many courses are needed and show the arithmetic you used.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read_workflow_route\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"version\\\":\\\"xray.workflow/1\\\",\\\"workflow\\\":\\\"discussion\\\",\\\"steps\\\":[\\\"Discuss capabilities or plans; do not claim project actions occurred.\\\"],\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Workflow selection only; no geometry, evidence or authority changed.\\\"}\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"use the project's roof-sheet coverage tool to get the authoritative arithmetic, then present the steps.\\n\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"calculate_draft_roof_sheet_coverage\",\"failed\":true,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"Invalid tool arguments: supplierReference: Invalid input: expected string, received undefined; : Unrecognized key: \\\"suplierReference\\\"\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"I had a typo in the parameter name. Let me retry with the correct field.\\n\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"calculate_draft_roof_sheet_coverage\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"projectId\\\":\\\"job-1bf6dd91-608b-4e4f-ab11-0a357875a38d\\\",\\\"projectRevision\\\":1,\\\"status\\\":\\\"draft-sheet-coverage\\\",\\\"columns\\\":14,\\\"courses\\\":2,\\\"sheets\\\":28,\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"developedWidthM\\\":\\\"10.0\\\",\\\"developedRunM\\\":\\\"9.8\\\",\\\"effectiveCoverM\\\":\\\"0.762\\\",\\\"orderLengthM\\\":\\\"5.0\\\",\\\"endLapM\\\":\\\"0.2\\\",\\\"measurementReference\\\":\\\"Rafter run 9.80 m supplied by the user for course calculation only; developed width and effective cover are illustrative (typical corrugated profile) and not user-specified — used only so the tool can run.\\\",\\\"supplierReference\\\":\\\"Sheet order length 5.000 m and end lap 0.200 m supplied by the user; supplier not named.\\\"},\\\"calculation\\\":{\\\"columns\\\":\\\"ceil(10.0 / 0.762) = 14\\\",\\\"coursesFormula\\\":\\\"run <= ordered length ? 1 : 1 + ceil((run - ordered length) / (ordered length - end lap))\\\",\\\"courses\\\":\\\"1 + ceil((9.8 - 5.0) / (5.0 - 0.2)) = 2\\\",\\\"coursesExpanded\\\":\\\"Course 1 covers a full ordered sheet length of 5.0 m. The remaining 4.8 m is covered by further courses that each add 5.0 - 0.2 = 4.8 m, so ceil(4.8 / 4.8) = 1 more course(s), giving 2 courses in total.\\\",\\\"courseBoundary\\\":\\\"2 course(s) cover any run greater than 5 m and up to and including exactly 9.8 m. A run of 9.800000001 m or more needs at least 3 courses.\\\",\\\"boundaryPrecision\\\":\\\"The next boundary value uses this calculator's nine-decimal-place input resolution in metres. It does not establish measurement accuracy or PDF coordinate precision.\\\",\\\"maxRunAtThisCourseCountM\\\":9.8,\\\"minRunForAnotherCourseM\\\":9.800000001,\\\"wrongFormulaWarning\\\":\\\"Do NOT compute courses as ceil(run / (ordered length - end lap)); for this input that would give 3 instead of the correct 2, because the first course is not shortened by an end lap.\\\",\\\"sheets\\\":\\\"14 columns × 2 courses = 28 sheets\\\",\\\"orderedLength\\\":\\\"28 sheets × 5.0 m = 140 m\\\",\\\"endLapPolicy\\\":\\\"The first course covers a full ordered sheet length. Each additional course adds ordered length minus end lap.\\\",\\\"excessRun\\\":\\\"9.8 m covered run - 9.8 m requested run = 0 m excess run. This is geometric over-coverage along the run, not a per-sheet waste or cutting quantity.\\\"},\\\"cuttingSchedule\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"not-calculated\\\",\\\"perSheetWasteM\\\":null,\\\"reusableOffcuts\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No cutting layout, trimming or offcut reuse is supplied. Do not infer per-sheet waste, scrap, usable cut length or reusable offcuts from coverage excess, in either the answer or Developer review.\\\"},\\\"orderedLinearM\\\":140,\\\"coveredWidthM\\\":10.668,\\\"coveredRunM\\\":9.8,\\\"excessWidthM\\\":0.668,\\\"excessRunM\\\":0,\\\"measurementReference\\\":\\\"Rafter run 9.80 m supplied by the user for course calculation only; developed width and effective cover are illustrative (typical corrugated profile) and not user-specified — used only so the tool can run.\\\",\\\"supplierReference\\\":\\\"Sheet order length 5.000 m and end lap 0.200 m supplied by the user; supplier not named.\\\",\\\"verifiedQuoteEligible\\\":false,\\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"End lap (the lengthwise lap between courses, also called a transverse lap) IS included in this calculation: every course after the first is shortened by the supplied end lap. Do not describe end laps or transverse laps as excluded.\\\",\\\"Side lap (the lap between adjacent sheets across the width) is NOT calculated here: it is already contained in the supplied effective sheet cover, so it is neither added nor deducted again. Side lap and end lap are separate laps and must be explained separately.\\\",\\\"One rectangular developed surface with identical ordered sheet lengths; no opening deductions, hips, valleys, cutting or reusable offcut schedule.\\\",\\\"No fixings, flashings, product suitability or compliance calculation. References are retained but not validated; draft and not eligible for verified quotes.\\\"]}\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"## Course count\\n\\nTwo courses.\\n\\n## Arithmetic (the way the tool works)\\n\\n1. First course = full ordered sheet length, so it covers 5.000 m of run — no end lap is deducted from the first course.\\n2. Remaining run = 9.800 − 5.000 = 4.800 m.\\n3. Every course after the first adds (ordered length − end lap) = 5.000 − 0.200 = 4.800 m of effective run.\\n4. Additional courses = ceil(4.800 / 4.800) = ceil(1.000) = 1.\\n5. Total courses = 1 (first) + 1 (additional) = 2.\\n\\n## Common trap to avoid\\n\\nDo not compute `ceil(run / (ordered length − end lap))` = `ceil(9.8 / 4.8)` = `ceil(2.042)` = 3. That overcounts by one because the first course is not shortened by an end lap.\\n\\n## Boundary for these exact inputs\\n\\nTwo courses cover any run greater than 5 m and up to exactly 9.800 m. A run of 9.800000001 m or more needs at least 3 courses. To check a different run, recalculate — do not predict.\\n\\n## Caveats\\n\\n- This is end-lap (also called transverse-lap) coverage along the run and is included in the course count. Side lap is already inside the supplied effective cover and is a separate lap — do not describe end or transverse laps as excluded.\\n- No cutting layout, per-sheet waste, offcuts, hips, valleys, openings or fixings are calculated here. Only the course count for the run is supplied.\\n- Draft calculation only; not eligible for a verified quote.\\n\\n## Developer review\\n\\n- **Outcome:** Answered clearly — 2 courses, with correct first-course-is-full arithmetic and the wrong-formula trap flagged.\\n- **Friction:** Tool needs width/cover for run-only questions; I labelled those illustrative, which adds noise.\\n- **Improvement:** A run-only mode would let course-count questions run without illustrative width inputs.\"}]}"

